    "text": "To determine the units digit of the sum \\(3^1 + 3^3 + 3^5 + 3^7 + \\ldots + 3^{2009}\\), we need to analyze the units digits of the powers of 3 and identify any patterns.\n\nFirst, let's compute the units digits of the first few powers of 3:\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n3^1 & = 3 \\quad \\text{(units digit is 3)} \\\\\n3^2 & = 9 \\quad \\text{(units digit is 9)} \\\\\n3^3 & = 27 \\quad \\text{(units digit is 7)} \\\\\n3^4 & = 81 \\quad \\text{(units digit is 1)} \\\\\n3^5 & = 243 \\quad \\text{(units digit is 3)} \\\\\n3^6 & = 729 \\quad \\text{(units digit is 9)} \\\\\n3^7 & = 2187 \\quad \\text{(units digit is 7)} \\\\\n3^8 & = 6561 \\quad \\text{(units digit is 1)} \\\\\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\n\nWe observe that the units digits repeat every 4 terms: 3, 9, 7, 1. Therefore, the units digits of \\(3^n\\) for \\(n \\geq 1\\) are periodic with a period of 4.\n\nNext, we need to consider the exponents in the given sum: \\(3^1, 3^3, 3^5, 3^7, \\ldots, 3^{2009}\\). These exponents form an arithmetic sequence with the first term \\(a = 1\\) and common difference \\(d = 2\\).\n\nTo find the number of terms in this sequence, we use the formula for the \\(n\\)-th term of an arithmetic sequence:\n\\[\na_n = a + (n-1)d\n\\]\nSetting \\(a_n = 2009\\):\n\\[\n2009 = 1 + (n-1) \\cdot 2\n\\]\n\\[\n2009 = 1 + 2n - 2\n\\]\n\\[\n2009 = 2n - 1\n\\]\n\\[\n2010 = 2n\n\\]\n\\[\nn = 1005\n\\]\n\nThus, there are 1005 terms in the sequence.\n\nNow, we need to determine the units digits of these 1005 terms by grouping them into complete cycles of 4:\n\\[\n\\frac{1005}{4} = 251 \\text{ remainder } 1\n\\]\n\nThis means there are 251 complete cycles of 4 terms, and 1 additional term. The units digits of these 251 complete cycles are:\n\\[\n3, 9, 7, 1\n\\]\n\nThe sum of the units digits in one complete cycle (3, 9, 7, 1) is:\n\\[\n3 + 9 + 7 + 1 = 20\n\\]\n\nThe units digit of 20 is 0. Therefore, the sum of the units digits of 251 complete cycles is:\n\\[\n251 \\times 0 = 0\n\\]\n\nNow, we need to add the units digit of the 1 additional term, which is \\(3^1 = 3\\). Thus, the units digit of the sum is:\n\\[\n0 + 3 = 3\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the units digit of \\(3^1 + 3^3 + 3^5 + 3^7 + \\ldots + 3^{2009}\\) is \\(\\boxed{3}\\).",
